1. A nozzle apparatus comprising:  

   a nozzle body defining a chamber, a fluid inlet communicating with the chamber, and a fluid outlet;  

   a plunger disposed in the chamber and movable relative to the nozzle body between a downstream position and an upstream position, the plunger including a seal that sealingly engages the nozzle body;  

   a prodder operatively connected to the plunger and configured to open the fluid outlet in response to movement of the plunger toward the upstream position; and  

   a biasing member configured to urge the plunger toward the downstream position,  

   wherein admission of pressurized fluid through the fluid inlet fills the chamber and moves the sealed plunger toward the upstream position against the biasing member, thereby causing the prodder to open the fluid outlet and permit discharge of the fluid from the chamber through the fluid outlet, and wherein a resulting reduction in fluid pressure within the chamber permits the biasing member to move the plunger toward the downstream position and cause the fluid outlet to reseal.

### Title  
**Pulsed Pressurized-Fluid Nozzle with Coordinated Valve and Spring-Biased Plunger**

### Abstract  
A pulsed-fluid nozzle assembly includes a nozzle body defining a pressurizable chamber and a discharge outlet. A plunger is movably disposed within the chamber and is sealingly engaged with an annular sealing member. A biasing member urges the plunger toward a predetermined position. A prodder-actuated valve selectively controls fluid communication between a source of pressurized fluid and the chamber. Operation of the valve is coordinated with reciprocating movement of the plunger such that pressure is cyclically accumulated and released within the chamber, thereby producing a succession of high-velocity fluid pulses through the discharge outlet.

### Exemplary Independent Claim  
1. **A pulsed-fluid nozzle assembly comprising:**  
   a nozzle body defining a chamber and a discharge outlet in fluid communication with the chamber;  
   a plunger disposed within the chamber for reciprocating movement relative to the nozzle body;  
   an annular seal arranged between the plunger and the nozzle body to provide a substantially fluid-tight sliding interface;  
   a biasing member operatively coupled to the plunger and configured to urge the plunger toward a predetermined position;  
   a prodder-actuated valve configured to selectively place the chamber in fluid communication with a source of pressurized fluid; and  
   a coordination mechanism configured to coordinate operation of the prodder-actuated valve with movement of the plunger so as to cyclically pressurize and discharge fluid from the chamber through the discharge outlet as a succession of high-velocity pulses.

### Exemplary Method Claim  
2. **A method of generating successive fluid pulses from a nozzle, the method comprising:**  
   supplying pressurized fluid to a chamber of the nozzle under control of a prodder-actuated valve;  
   displacing, in response to pressure within the chamber, a spring-biased plunger sealingly supported by an annular seal;  
   coordinating actuation of the prodder-actuated valve with reciprocation of the plunger to alternately accumulate and release pressure within the chamber; and  
   discharging fluid through an outlet of the nozzle during successive pressure-release cycles to generate a sequence of high-velocity fluid pulses.
